# Image digests for the capacity run.
#
# Immutable repository@sha256: references. `latest` is never used: a mutable tag
# is how an earlier attempt ran code from a revision that had not been tested.
# With all three present the guest pulls exactly these and compiles nothing, so
# the measurement server's CPU credits are not spent on a ~58 minute build.
#
# PROVENANCE - read this rather than assuming the digests match the branch head.
#
# These were built by CI run 42886156846 from merge commit
# 6716baf31986d9c45eeb4bc5455410bb2968bd06. They do NOT correspond to the
# current branch head: CI republishes on every run, keyed by the synthetic merge
# commit, so each run produces different digests for the same application source.
# The application source is unchanged since 6716baf (only orchestration scripts
# and documentation have changed), but that is a statement about source, not a
# claim that these digests were built from the launched commit.
#
# Before an approved launch, refresh these three values from the digest artifact
# of the CI run on the commit being launched. docs/results/stage3/image-provenance.md
# records the procedure and the exact form.
FIXTURE_API_DIGEST="ghcr.io/bhaveshsab/assetflow-capacity-api@sha256:29c7c3748239958ae83c6f4238ca9ac16ac5075cad7ddf5afe85333cc025f130"
FIXTURE_MIGRATE_DIGEST="ghcr.io/bhaveshsab/assetflow-capacity-migrate@sha256:c10658535ea7e7d4092297921a405562801bda6286ec0b641d68000042faecb1"
FIXTURE_WEB_DIGEST="ghcr.io/bhaveshsab/assetflow-capacity-web@sha256:17d15ee19b8cc918c97da1b81aa6aa60a98442c04acca9b953a416afca4abc75"
